00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
16 years after the series debut and nine  years after the last numbered entry  saintero is back and looking to reinvent  itself even though the announcement of  the game's new city and drastically  different cast of characters left fans  divided the experience is still looking  to be as wild as previous entries just  don't expect super powers this time  around here's everything we know about  saints row so far  the saints row series is starting from  scratch and so are you as the  protagonist instead of joining a gang  that has already been established you'll  be making a name for yourself and  building up to what will become the  legendary saints however don't think of  this as a prequel to the original game  with this opportunity to start over  series developer volition wanted to  create criminals that were more  relatable and one way of doing that was  to show those goons starting from  nothing the team also thought it was  crucial to introduce new characters due  to major changes in saints row 4 which i  won't spoil here but if you know you  know so who are the new soon to be  saints let's start with the business  mastermind eli who cares more about  making money than how the money is made  next is the getaway driver nina who  basically sounds like the just one more  job and i'm done type because of her  family history with gangs and how she  wants to leave that lifestyle behind and  then there's the gang's people pleaser  kevin who's actually a part of another  gang the idols when you meet him in the  game and finally the leader aka your  character aka the boss ultimately you'll  get to decide who the boss is and what  they do but according to volition the  boss can be described as an  overconfident person that doesn't like  to follow orders each of the new  criminals are just trying to make ends  meet and head out on their own because  they're tired of working for other gangs  their goal is to get rich and take over  the fictional city of santo aliso a huge  and vibrant sandbox in the american  southwest santo aliso will feature a  whole new set of radio stations as well  as familiar and new stores to customize  your boss to your heart's content  like previous games in the series saints  row's gameplay loop revolves around  seizing territory from rival gangs those  gangs include the muscle vehicle and  exercise obsessed los panteros the  anarchist nightclub owners known as the  idols and the private military  corporation martial defense industries  in order to expand your criminal empire  you'll be engaging in a bunch of  different activities including main  quests side quests as well as a new  activity called criminal ventures this  new type of activity will have you doing  things like taking over businesses  across the city to use as a front for  illegal activities gunplay and traversal  are what we've come to expect from the  series however now you'll have more  options when it comes to vehicle combat  from side swiping your enemies to  hopping on top of your car and firing  back as you surf on it there are  multiple ways to take down your foes  while moving there is also the addition  of a wingsuit so players can fly around  the city for fun or eject themselves  from a car open the wingsuit and escape  the scene in style and speaking of style  volition claims to have created the  biggest customization suite of any  saints row game so far and based on one  of the latest trailers i'd say they were  definitely telling the truth with the  new game's in-depth character creator  you'll be able to change nearly  everything about your boss of course  there are tons of clothing options as  well as the return of layered clothing  but in saints row you'll also be able to  customize your skin down to the details  like texture glossiness color veins  scars tans body hair etc you can also  change the features of your entire face  and make it asymmetrical a new addition  to the series and the deep customization  doesn't stop at your character's body  there are also a lot of ways to  personalize the game's vehicles and  weapons as well but will we be able to  have the voice of nolan north i guess  we'll have to wait and see  like previous games in the series saints  row will feature drop in and drop out  cooperative online multiplayer allowing  for you and one other friend to team up  and play together completing missions  while in co-op will transfer over to  your own save so you won't waste time or  lose your boss character's progression  while playing in someone else's game so  if you've just started and you play a  late game mission with a buddy the game  will remember that and not force you to  play that mission over again once you  reach it in your own save  volition plans on releasing three  post-launch expansions for saints row  all of which will be included in the  game's expansion pass they haven't  revealed details about the packs just  yet but we're sure they'll be filled  with mayhem make sure to subscribe to  gamespot so you can get the details when  they're announced  similar to the rest of the series saints  row is being developed by volition and  published by deep silver in an interview  chief creative officer jim boone  mentioned the team at volition used a  handful of action films as reference  points for the reboot films like baby  driver for its vehicular movement hobbs  and shaw for its extravagance and john  wick for its stylized combat jim also  added that today's social climate has  outgrown the tone of prior saints games  aka moving away from sex toys as a  weapon was a bit of a needed change when  it comes to the game's voice talents the  team has only revealed bryce charles the  voice actor for the default boss  saints row will be releasing for both  current and past generation consoles as  well as pc so you'll be able to pick it  up on xbox series x and s xbox one ps4  and 5 and pc via the epic game store  saints row is scheduled to launch on  august 23rd 2022 the game was originally  set to release on february 25th before  being delayed so that the team could do  a little more fine-tuning and honestly  moving it out of february probably paid  off for them as the world was engrossed  with a little game called elden ring  saints row is available for pre-order  both through the game's website and  select online retailers there are three  physical additions to the game standard  which is sixty dollars criminal customs  also sixty dollars and notorious for  ninety dollars there are also three  digital versions of the game standard 60  gold for 90 and platinum for 100 all six  editions have the idols and archie pack  as a pre-order bonus but you'll also get  the saints criminal custom pack for  pre-ordering the criminal customs  notorious gold or platinum editions the  physical criminal customs edition adds  the saints criminal customs pack so it's  basically just an edition designed to  give you an extra bonus for pre-ordering  the game since it costs the same as the  standard edition you might as well grab  the criminal customs edition if you're  planning on pre-ordering the game anyway  finally the notorious edition adds the  expansion pass and comes with physical  collectibles including a steelbook case  like the physical version the digital  version of the standard edition only  includes the base game the gold edition  adds the los panteros american muscle  bundle and the expansion pass the  platinum edition includes all that plus  a digital copy of saints row the third  remastered  so let's recap the new saints row  features new characters a new city  deeper customization new vehicle combat  a wingsuit and loads of ways to cause  mayhem as you rise to the top of the  criminal food chain and there you have  it all of the information that's  currently available for saints row we've  still got a ways to go before august  23rd so expect more details to drop in  the lead up to release make sure you  subscribe to gamespot so you don't miss  out on any of the new updates as well as  our review when it's time you can find  me on social media at devonta chisholm  thanks for watching  you
 

